atthasallāpika:
[Attha+sallāpikā]  CL=8 One who is skilled in expressing cause and effect, and in responding to causal matters;
One who is skilled in reciprocal dialogue between two persons;
One who is skilled in presenting conversations spoken between two individuals.

atthasandassana:
[Attha+sandassana]  CL=8 in feminine gender Atthasandassani)
(1) One who clearly explains or teaches the results (beneficial dhammas);
(2) One who is skilled in presenting the benefits (or advantages).

atthasādhaka:
[Attha+sādhaka]  CL=8 In feminine Atthasādhikā)
(1) One who is capable of bringing about a result (benefit);
(2) Stealing that is capable of bringing about a result — namely, the result of pārājika (defeat) even before the matter of the theft is concluded — one type among the 25 forms of stealing.
